/**
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * CURATED SOURCES  —  edit this file to add/remove feed sources
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Each object in the SOURCES array describes one tab in the UI.
 * The /scrape Edge Function is an RSS GENERATOR — point `url` at ANY
 * web page and it builds a feed from it (like rss.app):
 *
 *   1. If `url` is already an RSS / Atom / RDF feed, it is parsed directly.
 *   2. Otherwise the page's HTML is fetched and a feed is GENERATED by
 *      heuristically extracting headline links, summaries and dates.
 *      No per-site CSS selectors are required.
 *
 * FIELDS
 * ──────
 * id      — Unique key used internally (no spaces, lowercase)
 * name    — Label shown on the tab button
 * url     — Any web page URL (feed or normal page — both work)
 *
 * summarySelector — OPTIONAL CSS selector for a summary/overview element
 *                   on the source page. When present, the matched element's
 *                   content is shown as a banner ABOVE the article cards.
 *                   Example: '#market-summary > .overview-block'
 *
 * filterCriteria  — Rules applied after the feed is generated:
 *   keywords        — Keep only articles whose title contains at least one word.
 *   excludeKeywords — Drop articles whose title contains any of these words.
 *   minLength       — Minimum character count for the title to be included.
 *
 * TIPS
 * ────
 * • Any URL works, but cleaner pages (article listings, section fronts)
 *   generate better feeds than busy homepages full of navigation.
 * • To add a source, copy an object below and change the fields.
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 */

